  "body": "Found while building a test kit for PR #583 (2026-11-09).\n\n**Today:**\n- **What happens:** the Tormach post writes the machine's model name straight into the program's first comment. A machine named `Tormach 770MX (mm)` posted `(Tormach 770MX (mm))`.\n- **Why it breaks:** LinuxCNC (PathPilot) refuses a comment nested inside a comment, so the program fails to load. Machine names come from user-editable .mch files (#478's Machines editor), so this is reachable.\n- **Other posts:** they probably have the same pattern (Fanuc, Haas and Mazak write `(<machine>)` after `O0001`).\n\n**Expected:** every text a post writes inside a comment (machine name, operation name, tool description, program comment) is sanitised to that dialect's comment-legal characters: no `(` or `)` in ISO comments, no `;` in Heidenhain, and so on. Or the name is refused when the machine file is saved.\n\n**Done means:** a test per post with a machine and an operation whose names contain `(`/`)` posts a program whose comments parse; existing goldens are unchanged.\n\nRelated: #258 / PR #564 (program comment: it refuses `( )` at entry), #478.",
